IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P6-art-50: Chapter IV, Article 50, transparency obligations for providers and deployers of certain AI systems
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744; the consolidated text of 27.7.2026 is a rendering with no legal effect).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every function takes `the date asked` first. A result of NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTHING-kind);
-- JUST FALSE is the text's own no (FALSE-kind); JUST TRUE says the paragraph's obligation (or power) arises on the facts.
-- Article 50 is in the provision group General (applies from 2 August 2026, Art 113 second paragraph). Article 111(2) can save a legacy
-- high-risk AI system (keel fork F-111-2-all-groups), so every function about one AI system takes the keel's `AI system` record
-- (placement date, route, significant change) and passes it to the keel's applicability function.
-- Article 111(4) (inserted by the Omnibus) gives providers of synthetic-content systems placed before 2 August 2026 until 2 December 2026 for Article 50(2).
-- A defined term is a BOOLEAN input named for the definition (the seat computes it with the keel's Art 3 function).

§ `Article 50: when the group General applies`

-- The group General applies from 2 August 2026 (both versions of Art 113). A question about one AI system passes the system, so that Art 111(2) can save it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 50 the group General applies to the AI system on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) (`the AI system`'s `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

-- A provision that is not about one AI system (paragraphs 6 and 7) passes the core's constants.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 50 the group General applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- Seam S14 (PLAN.md section 4): Article 2(2) leaves out of an AI system classified as high-risk under Article 6(1), related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I,
-- every provision that its list does not name. Article 50 is not on the list in either text, so the keel's function answers JUST FALSE for every paragraph of it, and NOTHING where the route is not Article 6(1)
-- or the products are not Section B products; Article 50 then answers on its own provision. This helper is TRUE exactly where the keel answers JUST FALSE.
-- Article 50 is not one of Articles 57, 58 and 59, the only provisions whose answer reads "the requirements have been integrated", so that last argument cannot change the answer and is passed as FALSE
-- (both values are tested below). Paragraphs 6 and 7 do not call this helper (fork F-S14-reach).
-- src:41 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply. Articles 57, 58 and 59 shall apply only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420 | 2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply. Article 57 applies only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation.
@ref Art 2(2) applied to Article 50 (src:41) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:420)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paragraph of Article 50` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 50 Article 2(2) leaves the paragraph out for the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `route`) `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` FALSE `the reference to the paragraph` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the reference to the paragraph` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
            `number` IS 50
            `letter` IS ""
            `paragraph` IS `the paragraph of Article 50`

DECLARE `Art 50 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 50(1) ensure that the natural persons concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system`
    `Art 50(2) ensure that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated`
    `Art 50(3) inform the natural persons exposed to the operation of the system`
    `Art 50(3) process the personal data in accordance with the data protection instruments`
    `Art 50(4) disclose that the content has been artificially generated or manipulated`
    `Art 50(4) disclose that the text has been artificially generated or manipulated`

DECLARE `Art 50(7) official` IS ONE OF
    `Art 50(7) the AI Office`
    `Art 50(7) the Commission`

DECLARE `Art 50(7) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 50(7) encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice at Union level`
    `Art 50(7) assess whether adherence to the codes of practice is adequate`

§ `Article 50(1): AI systems intended to interact directly with natural persons`

-- src:753 | 1. Providers shall ensure that AI systems intended to interact directly with natural persons are designed and developed in such a way that the natural persons concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system, unless this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use. This obligation shall not apply to AI systems authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences, subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties, unless those systems are available for the public to report a criminal offence.
@ref Art 50(1) first and second sentences (src:753)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that authorisation is subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is available for the public to report a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 50(1) the provider must ensure that the natural persons concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 50 the group General applies to the AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter IV applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) can save a legacy high-risk system
        IF `Art 50 Article 2(2) leaves the paragraph out for the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` 1
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (Article 2(2), to an AI system classified as high-risk under Article 6(1) and related to products covered by the Section B legislation; Article 50 is not on the list; fork F-S14-reach)
        IF NOT `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "AI systems intended to interact directly with natural persons"
        IF `this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use"
        IF     `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences`
           AND `that authorisation is subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties`
           AND (NOT `the AI system is available for the public to report a criminal offence`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This obligation shall not apply to AI systems authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences, subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties, unless those systems are available for the public to report a criminal offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. Article 50(5) gives its time: "at the latest at the time of the first interaction or exposure". Day 0 of the trace is that day.
@ref Art 50(1) with Art 50(5) (the time)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that authorisation is subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is available for the public to report a criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 50 act`
`Art 50(1) the provider's duty to ensure that the natural persons concerned are informed` MEANS
    IF `Art 50(1) the provider must ensure that the natural persons concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` `this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use` `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` `that authorisation is subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties` `the AI system is available for the public to report a criminal offence` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 50(1) ensure that the natural persons concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the natural persons concerned were not informed at the latest at the time of the first interaction (Article 50(5))"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

§ `Article 50(2): synthetic audio, image, video or text content`

-- Article 111(4): a provider of an AI system generating synthetic content that was placed on the market before 2 August 2026 has until 2 December 2026 "to comply with Article 50(2)".
-- The keel's function gives that date (as amended only) or NOTHING; no date means the obligation is due when the group applies.
@ref Art 111(4), the time for Art 50(2)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 50(2) the date for compliance under Article 111(4) has come` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 111(4) the date by which the provider of an AI system generating synthetic content must comply with Article 50(2)` `the date asked` (`the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`) `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST `the deadline` THEN `the date asked` AT LEAST `the deadline`

-- src:754 | 2. Providers of AI systems, including general-purpose AI systems, generating synthetic audio, image, video or text content, shall ensure that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated. Providers shall ensure their technical solutions are effective, interoperable, robust and reliable as far as this is technically feasible, taking into account the specificities and limitations of various types of content, the costs of implementation and the generally acknowledged state of the art, as may be reflected in relevant technical standards. This obligation shall not apply to the extent the AI systems perform an assistive function for standard editing or do not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof, or where authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences.
@ref Art 50(2) (the obligation, and its exceptions) (src:754)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 50(2) the provider must ensure that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 50 the group General applies to the AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter IV applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) can save a legacy high-risk system
        IF `Art 50 Article 2(2) leaves the paragraph out for the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` 2
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (Article 2(2), to an AI system classified as high-risk under Article 6(1) and related to products covered by the Section B legislation; Article 50 is not on the list; fork F-S14-reach)
        IF NOT `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers of AI systems, including general-purpose AI systems, generating synthetic audio, image, video or text content"
        IF `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing` OR `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This obligation shall not apply to the extent the AI systems perform an assistive function for standard editing or do not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof"
        IF `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or where authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences"
        IF NOT (`Art 50(2) the date for compliance under Article 111(4) has come` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 111(4) gives a provider of a system placed before 2 August 2026 until 2 December 2026
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Art 50(2) first sentence, with Art 111(4) (the time)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 50 act`
`Art 50(2) the provider's duty to ensure that the outputs are marked and detectable` MEANS
    IF `Art 50(2) the provider must ensure that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` `the AI system performs an assistive function for standard editing` `the AI system does not substantially alter the input data provided by the deployer or the semantics thereof` `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 50(2) ensure that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text: a late act still reads FULFILLED (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- The second sentence of Art 50(2): the standard the technical solutions must meet. "As far as this is technically feasible, taking into account the specificities and
-- limitations of various types of content, the costs of implementation and the generally acknowledged state of the art" is a judgment the text leaves to the provider's
-- circumstances: each quality is a plain input stated "as far as technically feasible". The marking and detectability of the first sentence is the first two inputs.
@ref Art 50(2) first and second sentences (what the marking and the technical solutions must be)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the outputs are detectable as artificially generated or manipulated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions are effective, as far as this is technically feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions are interoperable, as far as this is technically feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions are robust, as far as this is technically feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical solutions are reliable, as far as this is technically feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 50(2) the marking of the outputs and the technical solutions are what paragraph 2 requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 50 the group General applies to the AI system on the date asked` `the date asked` `the AI system`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter IV applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) can save a legacy high-risk system
    ELSE IF `Art 50 Article 2(2) leaves the paragraph out for the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` 2
         THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (Article 2(2), to an AI system classified as high-risk under Article 6(1) and related to products covered by the Section B legislation; Article 50 is not on the list; fork F-S14-reach)
         ELSE JUST (    `the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format`
                    AND `the outputs are detectable as artificially generated or manipulated`
                    AND `the technical solutions are effective, as far as this is technically feasible`
                    AND `the technical solutions are interoperable, as far as this is technically feasible`
                    AND `the technical solutions are robust, as far as this is technically feasible`
                    AND `the technical solutions are reliable, as far as this is technically feasible`)
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of AI systems ... shall ensure that the outputs of the AI system are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated. Providers shall ensure their technical solutions are effective, interoperable, robust and reliable as far as this is technically feasible" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

§ `Article 50(3): emotion recognition systems and biometric categorisation systems`

