§ `Article 50: the AI system falls under Article 50 (the seam S4 of PLAN.md section 4)`

-- PLAN.md names this input (`the AI system falls under Article 50`) for Articles 2(12), 111(4) and 99. The paragraphs describe the systems that Article 50 reaches: one intended to interact directly
-- with natural persons (1), one generating synthetic audio, image, video or text content (2), an emotion recognition or biometric categorisation system (3), one generating or manipulating a deep fake or
-- text published to inform the public (4). The exceptions are not applied: a system within a description "falls under" the Article even if an exception then lifts the obligation.
-- A FALSE here is "none of the four descriptions fits these facts": it is not the text's own no, and a caller must not read it as one (NOTES.md, Seams).
@ref Art 50(1) to (4), the descriptions of the systems
GIVEN `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is an emotion recognition system or a biometric categorisation system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system generates or manipulates image, audio or video content constituting a deep fake, or text published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 50 the AI system falls under Article 50` MEANS
        `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons`
     OR `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content`
     OR `the AI system is an emotion recognition system or a biometric categorisation system`
     OR `the AI system generates or manipulates image, audio or video content constituting a deep fake, or text published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest`
